       failed: the_two_call_sites_pass_the_same_four_numbers,
               the_shipped_ledger_carries_unreviewed_rows..., every_shipped_budget_is_exactly...
    M2 both call sites raise it to 1107 together
       failed: the_shipped_ledger_carries_unreviewed_rows..., every_shipped_budget_is_exactly...
       (the agreement case stays green, which is the point: it is not a restatement of the others)
    M3 both call sites set every cap far above the debt (5000/500/500/2000)
       failed: every_shipped_budget_is_exactly_at_the_measured_debt,
               the_shipped_ledger_carries_unreviewed_rows..., names_gates_with_nothing_to_gate
    M4 budgets read from the whole file instead of the command
       failed: test_a_prose_mention_of_a_flag_is_not_the_budget,
               test_a_file_that_never_runs_the_gate_is_an_error
    M4b anchoring dropped (reader starts at the top of the file)
       failed: the module does not load at all -- the real ci.yml's first line is a comment,
               so the window is one line and carries no flags (rc=1, no test result lines)
    M5 reader keeps reading past the end of the command
       failed: test_the_window_stops_at_the_command

M4b is worth keeping in the record for the shape of the failure rather than its severity: the first
attempt at it was reported as "killed" by a driver that only looked for `FAIL:` lines, and what had
actually happened was an import-time error and zero tests run. A mutation harness that cannot tell
"the tests failed" from "the tests never ran" is the same bug this section is about, one layer up.
